\nDetails\nCentral\n9 a.m. to 9 p.m.\nDirections\nNorthside\n10 a.m. to 8 p.m.\nDirections\nWhat readers said\nFinally, I can study after work.\nThe library board will review attendance in the fall. A long-standing complaint among students and working parents was that the reading rooms closed before most people finished their day, so the extended schedule is intended to make the collections, the public computers, and the quiet study spaces available at the times when the community actually needs them, according to the library director.\n1. Board vote in March\n2. Hiring in April\n3. Review in October\nRelated stories\n• Council approves library budget\n• Spring book fair returns\n© 2026 Riverside Gazette. Contact us","caret":0,"selection":[0,1462],"font":{"family":"Times New Roman","size_tenths":120,"bold":false,"italic":false,"underline":true,"alignment":"left","color":{"r":0,"g":0,"b":238},"background":{"r":255,"g":255,"b":255}},"word":[0,10]},"top_window_title":"City Library Expands Evening Hours - Riverside Gazette - Google Chrome","top_window_class":"Chrome_WidgetWin_1"}
